<pkgmetadata>
  <longdescription>
    GLib-based Android binder client library.
    Required by Waydroid for Android container IPC via the binder protocol.
  </longdescription>
  <!--
    License evidence (audited 2026-08-25 against the pinned tarball,
    SHA512 as recorded in Manifest):

      LICENSE file: 3-clause BSD
      https://github.com/mer-hybris/libgbinder/blob/e176ef0c507898fbe7f3fdd1bb4955f2adaf370f/LICENSE

      Copyright (C) 2025 Jolla Mobile Ltd.
      Copyright (C) 2018-2025 Slava Monich <slava@monich.com>
      Copyright (C) 2018-2024 Jolla Ltd.

    125 of 186 files carry the same 3-clause BSD header; no GPL, LGPL,
    MIT or Apache notice appears anywhere in the tree. rpm/libgbinder.spec
    and debian/copyright both declare BSD, consistent with LICENSE.

    src/binder.h is a bionic-scrubbed copy of the Linux UAPI binder header
    and carries the standard AOSP notice stating it contains no
    copyrightable information.

    Gentoo's "BSD" license file is the 3-clause text, so LICENSE="BSD" is
    the correct declaration; Gentoo has no "BSD-3" alias.
  -->
  <upstream>
    <remote-id type="github">mer-hybris/libgbinder</remote-id>
  </upstream>
